---
// Free Launch Preflight for founders: checks a domain's public DNS (email authentication, inbox readiness, basic
// domain hygiene) right in the browser through Cloudflare's public DNS-over-HTTPS resolver. Nothing is stored or
// sent to NeonKey; the only request leaves the browser for cloudflare-dns.com (allowed in public/_headers).
// Founders track (Nov 6 2026): kept apart from the small-business pages, linked only from /founders/ and the footer.
import { url } from '../../config';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import DomainCheck from '../../components/DomainCheck.astro';
import { setupGuide, emailLockdown, usd } from '../../data/services';
---
<Base title="Free Launch Preflight for founders" description="Free check for founders: see if your domain's email will land before you send a launch email or cold outreach. SPF, DKIM, DMARC, MX and more, in seconds. Nothing is stored.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Free tool · For founders" title="Launch Preflight" crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { href: '/founders/', label: 'Founders' }, { label: 'Launch Preflight' }]}>
    <p class="lede">Before your launch email or first cold outreach goes out, check that your domain is set up so inboxes trust it. Type your domain and get a plain report with what to fix first.</p>
    <Fragment slot="meta">
      <li><span>Free</span></li>
      <li><span>No signup</span></li>
      <li><span>Runs in your browser</span></li>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHeader>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container narrow-ish">
      <DomainCheck placeholder="yourstartup.com" track="founders">
        <div slot="next" class="panel topline accent-magenta pf-next">
          <h2 class="pf-h">What to do next</h2>
          <p><strong>Want it fixed for you?</strong> The <a href={url('/services/email-lockdown/')} data-umami-event="preflight-cta" data-umami-event-target="lockdown" data-umami-event-track="founders">Email Authentication Setup</a> ({usd(emailLockdown.from)}) checks your records and hands you the exact ones to add, with a PDF report.</p>
          <p><strong>Want to build the whole backend yourself?</strong> <a href={url('/founders/guide/')} data-umami-event="preflight-cta" data-umami-event-target="guide" data-umami-event-track="founders">{setupGuide.name}</a> is the step-by-step guide to the stack NeonKey runs on: domain and email, website, Stripe, a product that delivers itself, outreach and lead tracking. An Email Authentication Setup is included.</p>
        </div>
      </DomainCheck>

      <div class="panel pf-about">
        <h2 class="pf-h">What this checks</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>MX:</strong> whether your domain can receive mail, and which provider handles it.</li>
          <li><strong>SPF:</strong> the public list of services allowed to send as you, and whether it stays under the 10-lookup limit.</li>
          <li><strong>DKIM:</strong> a signing key for common providers (Google, Microsoft, Resend and others). We can only test well-known selector names, so a miss here isn't proof you have none.</li>
          <li><strong>DMARC:</strong> the policy that tells Gmail, Yahoo and Microsoft what to do with mail that fails, and whether you get reports.</li>
          <li><strong>Extras:</strong> MTA-STS, TLS reporting and CAA, the small records that harden a domain.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted">Passing all of these doesn't guarantee the inbox. Content, volume, sending reputation and each provider's own filters matter too. It does remove the most common setup reasons mail gets filtered.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
